spec:
  grid: 10x10 [observed]
  background: 7 [observed]
  frame: optional 1-cell perimeter frame in a non-bg color (0 or 1 examples have it)
  sprites:
    count: 3-4
    type: monochrome 4-connected components (excluding frame)
    colors: each sprite has a single non-bg color; two sprites MAY share the same color if they are separate components
    areas: all areas must be distinct; range 1-12 per sprite
    bbox: 1-6 rows x 1-4 cols; density (area / bbox_area) >= 0.5
    non_rectangular: some sprites may have holes in their bbox (observed ~27%)
    placement: scattered freely on the bg; sprites may be 4-adjacent to each other
  packing_constraint: sum of sorted-sprite bbox widths <= grid width; max bbox height <= grid height
  output:
    clear grid to bg; sort sprites by area ascending
    paste bounding-box sprites left-to-right, bottom-aligned, no horizontal gaps between bbox columns

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Choose grid 10x10, bg=7.
    2. Generate 3-4 sprites with distinct areas (range 1-12). For each, pick a non-bg color and a 4-connected shape fitting in a small bbox (density >= 0.5).
    3. Sort sprites by area; verify sum of bbox widths <= 10 and max bbox height <= 10.
    4. Build the output by packing sprites left-to-right, bottom-aligned.
    5. To build the input, place each sprite at a random non-overlapping position on the bg grid. Optionally add a 1-cell perimeter frame in a new color.
    6. Ensure no sprite bbox overlaps another sprite's pixels (bg cells in bbox may overlap other bboxes).
